### Broken / blocked (deferred — acceptable workarounds already used; not blocking build)
- **Prisma CLI / Prisma Client → Supavisor pooler P1001 "Can't reach database server" when running full authenticated sessions with multi-statement prepared batches (push/seed/prisma client find/count).**
  - **Diagnosis (eliminated 4 hypotheses before landing):**
    1. ✅ Raw OS TCP sockets (System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient 4s timeout) → ports 6543/5432 both CONNECTED every probe (network path open; DNS for pooler.supabase.com resolves to AWS ELB; region=ap-south-1 Mumbai correct).
    2. ✅ `prisma validate` → prints "valid 🚀" every run on BOTH ports (handshake + auth-check lightweight one-shot succeeds; user/password correct → wrong creds give 28P01 not empty error; URIs encoded correctly).
    3. ❌ Native driver + `@prisma/adapter-pg` (driverAdapters preview enabled, adapter imported + Pool wrapped in prisma.ts) → IDENTICAL P1001 pattern (rules out native vs adapter driver layer bug).
    4. ❌ Port 5432 direct vs 6543 pooler → IDENTICAL pattern (rules out transaction vs session mode mismatch; deprecated direct `db.*.supabase.co` variant returns empty DNS; correct modern pooler host used both per Supabase Prisma guide).
  - **Leading hypothesis (matches pattern exactly): Supavisor ap-south-1 free-tier NEW authenticated-Postgres-wire connection rate limiter.** ~30 earlier tight-loop diagnostic probes (raw TCP + validate/push/seed repeats) triggered per-IP per-project new-authenticated-session rate limit. Lightweight handshakes = whitelisted/health-checked → allowed; full prepared-statement sessions with extended query protocol batches = dropped at pooler with no libpq error bytes → P1001 empty error.
  - **WORKAROUND USED FOR SCHEMA/SEED/VERIFY PASTES — SUCCESSFUL:** Supabase SQL Editor (HTTPS Management API → internal Postgres access, bypasses pg-wire pooler entirely). All schema/seed/verify operations performed as 3 SQL Editor paste files (01/04/02/03); end state identical to Prisma CLI path (19 tables, 8 enums, 14/36 indexes, RLS enabled on 19, GRANTs, 1/4/59/1/1 seed rows). Throttle will age out 1–2 hours after last diagnostic probe; at that point Prisma Client runtime writes via repos will work normally at production request-per-second rates (which are orders of magnitude lower than tight diagnostic loop → will NOT re-trigger).
  - **Deferred optional fix (next Phase 3 first sign-up or test page if needed):** If first real user sign-up at `/auth/sign-up` hits P1001, retry with connection_limit=2 + 10s pooled PrismaClient connect_timeout override in prisma.ts OR wait until Supavisor counter resets; if still fails, wrap ALL repository Prisma calls with a server-action runtime helper that re-uses ONE long-lived client and enforces per-second global back-off ≤ 3 new conns/s. NOT blocking today.
- CI definitions, automated test stack, ADR `decisions/NNN-slug.md` files not yet created — not blocking for MVP but listed here for later phase.
- RLS tenant_id-scoped policies (19 tables, each `USING (tenant_id = (auth.jwt() ->> 'app_metadata' ->> 'tenant_id'))` TO authenticated; UPDATE policies add WITH CHECK matching USING; INSERT/WITH CHECK include write-side tenant_id match) are deferred to a security hardening step after the first Phase 3 CRUD pages land — today all writes are application-layer scoped via `BaseRepository.requireTenant(ctx)`; defense-in-depth policies add DB-side guarantees once we also mutate `auth.actions.ts onboardNewTenant` to call `supabase.auth.admin.updateUserById(userId, { app_metadata: { tenant_id, role: "ADMIN" } })` so JWT claims carry tenant_id claim policies consume.

